course: dictionary
lesson: 7025
title: Names of people and spellings that change
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words name a group of people, like Parsee. Look at the clues around the word to see what kind of word it is: «A "Parsee" (today usually spelled Parsi) is one of the Parsi people» tells you it names a person from a community.
explain: A word can have more than one spelling. The dictionary says Parsee is also spelt Parsi, and today Parsi is the usual spelling. The story explains the change for you in brackets, so you do not have to guess.
explain: Clues also tell you whether a story is true or made up. «How the Rhinoceros Got His Skin» is a Just So Story, a made-up tale. The Parsee in it is a character who takes his revenge, so you can enjoy the story without thinking every part really happened.
explain: When you meet a word like this, ask three questions: Is it a name? Does the spelling look different? Is the text true or made up? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A Parsee is a member of a community of Zoroastrians in India and Pakistan.
fact: Parsi families came from Persia (Iran) more than a thousand years ago.
fact: «Parsee» is also spelt «Parsi», and today «Parsi» is the usual spelling.
fact: In «How the Rhinoceros Got His Skin», the Parsee is a man on an island in the Red Sea who wears a hat that shines in the sun.
fact: A Just So Story is a made-up tale that explains how something came to be, so the rhino's folded skin in the story is not a true explanation.
exercise: «The Parsee takes his revenge: he rubs the skin full of stale, tickly cake-crumbs.» What does revenge mean here? | *Getting even with someone who hurt you | Taking a long nap under a palm tree | Baking a big cake for the whole island | A thank-you gift for a friend
exercise: «A "Parsee" (today usually spelled Parsi) is one of the Parsi people.» What is the usual spelling today? | Parsey | Pearsy | *Parsi
exercise: «The Parsi families came to India from Persia long ago.» Where did they come from? | The Red Sea | An uninhabited island | *Persia (Iran) | Mumbai
test: «In this story he lives on "an uninhabited island".» What does uninhabited mean? | An island full of palm trees | A busy island full of people | An island with a big cake shop | *An island where nobody lives
test: In «How the Rhinoceros Got His Skin», what kind of explanation does the story give? | *A made-up explanation of why rhinos have folded skin | A history of the Red Sea | A recipe for cakes | A true report of a rhino's life
exam: A Parsi person follows which religion? | Hinduism | *Zoroastrianism | Buddhism | Christianity
